Title: HIGHWAY SONG
Credit: Written by
Author: Sample Writer
Draft date: Stage 2 departments sample - 02 November 2026

FADE IN:

EXT. HIGHWAY - NIGHT #1#

Rain pours down on an empty highway. RAGHAV (30s), soaked leather jacket, rides his battered Royal Enfield motorcycle through the rain. TARA (20s), in a red salwar kameez, rides pillion, arms around his waist.

Headlights flare behind them. INSPECTOR KHAN's police jeep gives chase, its siren wailing.

TARA
They're gaining on us!

RAGHAV
Hold on!

Raghav swerves off the road onto a dirt track. Tara's dupatta tears loose and flies away into the dark.

EXT. VILLAGE SQUARE - DAY #2#

SONG: "RANG DE RE" (PLAYBACK).

CRANE UP to reveal two hundred dancers in white kurtas filling the square, throwing coloured powder. Six dhol players pound out the rhythm. A crowd of villagers cheers from the rooftops.

Tara, in a green ghagra, dances at the centre, her face streaked with pink powder. Raghav pushes through the dancers to reach her.

A decorated white horse stands by the temple gate. Stray dogs bark at the drums.

TARA
(singing)
Rang de re, rang de re...

RAGHAV
Come with me tonight.

INT. POLICE STATION - DAY #3#

A cramped station. Through the window, Inspector Khan's police jeep is parked outside.

INSPECTOR KHAN (50s), in a starched khaki uniform, cleans his revolver at the desk. Two constables stand guard at the door.

Raghav sits handcuffed on a bench, still in his damp leather jacket.

A phone rings. Khan ignores it.

INSPECTOR KHAN
You ran from me, Raghav. Innocent men don't run.

RAGHAV
Innocent men don't trust you.

EXT. QUARRY - NIGHT #4#

Floodlights on a stone quarry. BHIM (40s), a prosthetic scar across his cheek, waits with several of his men.

Raghav and Bhim fight on the edge of the slope. Bhim kicks Raghav, who falls down the slope and rolls to a stop at the bottom. Raghav's shirt is torn and bloodied; a cut opens on his forehead.

Bhim fires at a fuel drum. It explodes into a ball of fire.

Three police jeeps screech into the quarry, sirens blaring.

BHIM
This isn't over!

INT. HOSPITAL ROOM - NIGHT #5#

A quiet hospital room. A heart monitor beeps steadily. An IV drip runs into Raghav's arm. His forehead is bandaged.

Tara sits beside the bed and softly sings a lullaby, unaccompanied.

TARA
(singing softly)
Soja, soja...

RAGHAV
You still remember that song.

EXT. TEMPLE STEPS - DAWN (1975) #6#

A vintage Ambassador car is parked at the foot of the temple steps. Temple bells ring. A cow wanders past.

DEV (30s), in 1970s bell-bottoms and a wide-collared shirt, climbs the steps carrying a brass lamp.

RAGHAV (V.O.)
My father came here every morning. Until the morning he didn't.

INT. RAGHAV'S HOUSE - NIGHT #7#

A small, dark room. A PRIEST in saffron robes, long fake beard, enters. It is Bhim in disguise.

Tara sits at the mirror and cuts off her long braid with scissors.

A gunshot rings out outside.

TARA
Who's there?

BHIM
Only a priest, child.

EXT. RAGHAV'S HOUSE - DAY #8#

AERIAL - DRONE: the house, now a burnt-out ruin, alone on a hillside. The house set is a full replica built on the backlot, burnt to its frame.

OLD RAGHAV (75), grey-haired and deeply wrinkled, sits on the step beside a golden retriever. In the yard, the battered Royal Enfield motorcycle stands rusting.

OLD RAGHAV
We made it, old boy.

FADE OUT.
